# DB_URL: Supabase *direct* connection string (port 5432), NOT the 6543
# transaction-mode pooler — the engine uses prepared statements, which that
# pooler breaks.
#
# TLS note: Supabase issues its own CA for database connections rather than a
# publicly-trusted certificate. That CA is compiled into the binary via
# include_bytes! (see src/main.rs), so nothing extra is needed at runtime here.
DB_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF:YOUR_PASSWORD@aws-0-YOUR_REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Upstash TCP connection string (Details -> Connection Strings -> redis://).
# The engine talks Redis directly; the Next.js app uses the REST pair instead.
REDIS_URL=rediss://default:YOUR_PASSWORD@YOUR_INSTANCE.upstash.io:6379

# This file is optional at runtime — main.rs loads it if present but does not
# require it, so CI can inject the two variables above as workflow secrets.
